    {
      "id": "engines-3",
      "title": "The engines and the brake-holding button (cont.)",
      "role": "proof",
      "topic": "powertrain",
      "outcome": "Choose an engine and gearbox combination",
      "usp_ids": [
        "choose-your-gears"
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "When traffic pauses, auto hold keeps the stationary car in place without keeping the brake pressed, standard on King, King Knight and Lounge; its button sits beside the parking-brake switch.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "image",
            "ref": "im_pdf_7f6a4cea202b824c4a74",
            "focus": "Auto hold button"
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F015",
            "F016"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "engines-L3",
          "start": 65.2,
          "duration": 15.8,
          "exact": false
        }
      ],
      "checkin": "",
      "deeper": [
        {
          "text": "For the one-point-five-litre turbo petrol, stated maximum power is 117.5 kilowatts, or 160 PS, at 5,500 revolutions per minute. PS is the source power unit. Its seven-speed dual-clutch automatic is listed only on King.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "image",
            "ref": "im_pdf_eb83000c135195546031",
            "focus": "Turbo power specification"
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F003",
            "F004",
            "F005",
            "F006"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "engines-D1"
        },
        {
          "text": "The one-point-five-litre diesel lists 250 newton metres of torque at 1,500 to 2,750 revolutions per minute. Torque describes engine twisting force. That specification does not establish loaded climbing performance or an acceleration time.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "image",
            "ref": "im_pdf_d62b85cb6c76c3c1a60e",
            "focus": "Diesel torque specification"
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F003",
            "F007"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "engines-D2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Auto hold additionally appears on S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatics. Modes and paddle shifters are automatic-only on S(O), S(O) Knight, SX Premium, King, King Knight and Lounge; the matrix currently lists no S(O) Knight automatic.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "ref": "im_pdf_7f6a4cea202b824c4a74",
            "focus": ""
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F013",
            "F014",
            "F016"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "engines-D3"
        }
      ],
      "stop_id": "powertrain",
      "fundamental": true,
      "word_budget": 30,
      "budget_source_id": "engines",
      "checkin_audio": null,
      "planned_seconds": 15.8,
      "start": 65.2,
      "duration": 15.8,
      "spoken": 15.8,
      "measured": false
