    {
      "id": "wheels",
      "title": "The wheels beneath the body",
      "role": "proof",
      "topic": "stance-and-ride",
      "outcome": "Choose wheel style without assuming comfort",
      "usp_ids": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Beneath the body, steel wheels start at the E trim and alloys at S(O). That's a choice of wheel style; comfort inside the cabin needs separate evidence.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "image",
            "ref": "im_pdf_f9bbe411c2dac4280a3e",
            "focus": "Wheels beneath body"
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F017"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "wheels-L1",
          "start": 81.0,
          "duration": 14.2,
          "exact": false
        }
      ],
      "checkin": "",
      "deeper": [
        {
          "text": "E and EX have R16 steel wheels with covers; EX(O) has R16 styled steel. S(O) has R17 black alloys, while SX and SX Premium have R17 diamond-cut alloys. This mapping identifies equipment, without a ride comparison.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "ref": "im_pdf_654ca5b2d4cb084d4a92",
            "focus": ""
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F017"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "wheels-D1"
        },
        {
          "text": "King has R18 diamond-cut alloys. S(O) Knight, King Knight and Lounge Edition have R18 matte-black alloys. A whole-car photograph does not establish which of those finishes is fitted to every other trim.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "image",
            "ref": "im_pdf_f9bbe411c2dac4280a3e",
            "focus": "Whole car profile"
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F017"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "wheels-D2"
        },
        {
          "text": "The listed tyre sizes are 205/65 R16 at entry level, 215/60 R17 on S(O), SX and SX Premium, and 215/55 R18 on S(O) Knight, King and King Knight. No ground-clearance or suspension specification is supplied here.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "ref": "im_pdf_654ca5b2d4cb084d4a92",
            "focus": ""
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F064"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "wheels-D3"
        }
      ],
      "stop_id": "stance-and-ride",
      "fundamental": true,
      "word_budget": 27,
      "planned_seconds": 14.2,
      "start": 81.0,
      "duration": 14.2,
      "spoken": 14.2,
      "measured": false
