    {
      "id": "space",
      "title": "The boot and the rear seatbacks",
      "role": "proof",
      "topic": "space-and-practicality",
      "outcome": "Arrange seating and luggage together",
      "usp_ids": [
        "share-the-room"
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Packing for a longer journey, the standard split rear seat layout balances passenger and storage space. Rear passengers can adjust their seatback angle from S(O), giving the seating arrangement another choice to consider.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "ref": "im_pdf_21bb72b4fd2c922acfa9",
            "focus": ""
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F022",
            "F023",
            "F021",
            "F024"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "space-L1",
          "start": 95.2,
          "duration": 17.4,
          "exact": false
        }
      ],
      "checkin": "",
      "deeper": [
        {
          "text": "The CRETA has five seats, with a standard sixty-forty split rear seat. Rear air vents and a rear centre armrest with cup holders are standard too. These specifications do not establish a rear-legroom measurement.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "ref": "im_pdf_8bfe17bdf06959cc1e40",
            "focus": ""
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F001",
            "F020",
            "F022",
            "F059"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "space-D1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rear seatback recline starts at S(O): S(O), S(O) Knight, SX, SX Premium, King, King Knight and Lounge have the two-step adjustment. Rear-window sunshades also include EX(O), extending that feature to a different starting trim.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "none",
            "ref": "",
            "focus": ""
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F021",
            "F024",
            "F060"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "space-D2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hyundai describes the boot as storage for luggage and travel essentials. I can't confirm a litre-capacity figure from these details. Using the actual bags is the useful personal fit check; the pictured luggage is an example.",
          "step": "say",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "image",
            "ref": "im_pdf_06dc900e0519722a9b8a",
            "focus": "Luggage in boot"
          },
          "fact_ids": [
            "F063"
          ],
          "card": "none",
          "delivery": {
            "tone": "warm",
            "pace": 1.0
          },
          "unverified": false,
          "id": "space-D3"
        }
      ],
      "stop_id": "space-and-practicality",
      "fundamental": true,
      "word_budget": 33,
      "planned_seconds": 17.4,
      "start": 95.2,
      "duration": 17.4,
      "spoken": 17.4,
      "measured": false
